# Test inputs and fixtures are bytes, never text: with core.autocrlf (Windows) git would
# rewrite line endings inside PDFs and EPUBs that contain no NUL byte, and checkouts would
# get corrupted files (and a test failing for no reason).
*.pdf binary
*.epub binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.sqlite binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
# Recorded Wikipedia fixtures are compared byte for byte.
tests/**/*.html -text
